sing or distributing child sexual abuse material (CSAM), or soliciting a minor are severe criminal offenses classified as child sexual abuse or exploitation, carrying harsh legal penalties. \n\n### Treatment and Prevention\nMedical and psychological professionals offer specialized interventions, such as cognitive-behavioral therapy (CBT) and, in some cases, anti-androgen medications to reduce sexual drive. The primary goal of clinical intervention is the prevention of harm, focusing on self-control, risk management, and preventing the individual from ever acting on inappropriate urges. In many regions, anonymous helplines and prevention initiatives exist to encourage individuals who experience these attractions to seek help before any harm occurs.",
