. Municipal Pet Disposal / Trash (Practical option)\nIf burial or cremation isn't an option:\n* Some municipal animal shelters or animal control departments accept deceased pets for disposal, sometimes for a small fee.\n* In some jurisdictions, putting small pets in the household trash is permitted, while in others it is prohibited. If you must use this route, double-wrap the body securely in plastic bags before placing it in the outdoor trash bin close to pickup day.\n\n### Temporary Storage\nIf you need time to decide or wait until you can reach a vet, wrap the body in a clean cloth, place it inside a sealed plastic bag or airtight container, and keep it in a very cold place (like a refrigerator, garage in winter, or surrounded by ice packs) to prevent natural decomposition until you can carry out your plans.",
