            "text": "Eliminating other players in *Call of Duty* depends on your weapons, positioning, and basic game mechanics. Here is a breakdown of the primary ways to get kills:\n\n### 1. Shooting (Firearms)\n* **Aim Down Sights (ADS):** Hold the aim button (Left Trigger / Right Mouse Button) to aim accurately before firing. Firing from the hip (Hipfire) is faster but much less accurate, unless you are at very close range with a shotgun or SMG.\n* **Target the Head/Upper Torso:** Headshots apply a damage multiplier, significantly reducing the Time-to-Kill (TTK). \n* **Control Recoil:** Pull your aim slightly downward while firing automatic weapons to compensate for the gun's upward kick.\n\n### 2. Melee Attacks\n* **Standard Melee:** Press the melee button (Right Stick on controller / 'E' or 'V' on mouse/keyboard) when close to an enemy to strike them with your weapon.\n* **Melee Weapons:** Equipping a knife, sledgehammer, or dual kodachis allows for one-hit kills at close range.\n* **Finishing Moves (Executions):** Sneak directly behind an enemy and **hold** the melee button. This triggers an unskippable execution animation.\n\n### 3. Lethal Equipment\n* **Frag Grenades:** Cook them (hold before throwing) so the enemy has less time to react.\n* **Semtex / Thermite:** Sticky explosives that eliminate players immediately if you land a direct hit.\n* **Throwing Knives:** A one-hit kill if you hit the upper body, useful for fast close-quarters combat.\n* **Claymores / Proximity Mines:** Place these near doorways or high-traffic choke points.\n\n### 4. Killstreaks / Scorestreaks\nEarning consecutive kills or points without dying unlocks powerful support:\n* **Direct Attack:** Precision Airstrike, Cruise Missile, or Chopper Gunner allow you to target clusters of enemies from above.\n* **Automated:** Sentries, Attack Helicopters, or VTOL jets will automatically track and eliminate targets within their line of sight.\n\n### General Combat Tips\n* **Use Your Mini-map:** Watch for red dots (enemies firing unsuppressed weapons) or use UAV streaks to reveal enemy locations.\n* **Centering:** Keep your crosshairs at chest/head level where you expect an enemy to appear, rather than looking at the ground while sprinting.\n* **Use Cover:** Never sprint around corners blindly; pie the corners and clear angles methodically.",
